  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "verse-001",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 1,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:1",
      "numberLabel": "1",
      "text": "Then Jonah prayed unto the LORD his God out of the fish’s belly,",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:1",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:1"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-002",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 2,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:2",
      "numberLabel": "2",
      "text": "And said, I cried by reason of mine affliction unto the LORD, and he heard me; out of the belly of hell cried I, and thou heardest my voice.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:2",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:2"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-003",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 3,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:3",
      "numberLabel": "3",
      "text": "For thou hadst cast me into the deep, in the midst of the seas; and the floods compassed me about: all thy billows and thy waves passed over me.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:3",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:3"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-004",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 4,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:4",
      "numberLabel": "4",
      "text": "Then I said, I am cast out of thy sight; yet I will look again toward thy holy temple.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:4",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:4"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-005",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 5,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:5",
      "numberLabel": "5",
      "text": "The waters compassed me about, even to the soul: the depth closed me round about, the weeds were wrapped about my head.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:5",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:5"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-006",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 6,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:6",
      "numberLabel": "6",
      "text": "I went down to the bottoms of the mountains; the earth with her bars was about me for ever: yet hast thou brought up my life from corruption, O LORD my God.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:6",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:6"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-007",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 7,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:7",
      "numberLabel": "7",
      "text": "When my soul fainted within me I remembered the LORD: and my prayer came in unto thee, into thine holy temple.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:7",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:7"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-008",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 8,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:8",
      "numberLabel": "8",
      "text": "They that observe lying vanities forsake their own mercy.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:8",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:8"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-009",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 9,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:9",
      "numberLabel": "9",
      "text": "But I will sacrifice unto thee with the voice of thanksgiving; I will pay that that I have vowed. Salvation is of the LORD.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:9",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:9"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "verse-010",
      "type": "bible_verse",
      "verse": 10,
      "verseId": "kjv:jonah:2:10",
      "numberLabel": "10",
      "text": "And the LORD spake unto the fish, and it vomited out Jonah upon the dry land.",
      "metadata": {
        "reference": "Jonah 2:10",
        "verseKey": "kjv:jonah:2:10"
      }
    }
  ],
  "source": {
